## Why This Matters
This interview question tests your understanding of macro correctness, multi-tenant schema templating, and CI/CD integration for data quality enforcement.

## Key Concepts
- dbt macros and singular/generic tests
- Per-tenant schemas using `analytics_{{tenant}}` naming convention
- CI gating: blocking deploys when any tenant's test reports NULL violations

## Code Example
```sql
-- analytics_base/macros/not_null_guard.sql
{% macro not_null_guard(tenant, model, col) %}
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM analytics_{{ tenant }}.{{ model }} WHERE {{ col }} IS NULL) = 0
{% endmacro %}
```

```sql
-- tests/generic/not_null_guard.sql
{% test not_null_guard(model, col) %}
  {% if execute %}
    {% set result = run_query(not_null_guard(this.name, model, col)) %}
    {% if result.rows[0][0] | int != 0 %}
      {% do exceptions.raise_compile_error(
        "Failed: " ~ model ~ "." ~ col ~ " contains NULL values"
      ) %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
{% endtest %}
```

The test verifies zero NULL values exist in the target column across all tenant-specific models.

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design an adaptive per-tenant pipeline, leveraging dbt macros to route between data paths, while keeping data consistent and isolated. It also probes how velocity-based decisions, late data, and lineage are codified in CI and tests.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant velocity in analytics_{{tenant}}.config
- Adaptive path selection: MERGE upsert vs FULL_REFRESH
- Idempotence with last_hash for dedup
- Late data handling (2-day window)
- Tests: not_null on (tenant_id, day, metric_id); unique constraint on (tenant_id, day, metric_id)
- Cross-tenant isolation via per-tenant schemas and RLS-like controls
- Global lineage tracking across adaptive paths

## Code Example

```sql
-- dbt macro sketch: select path per tenant
{% macro tenant_path(tenant) %}
  {% set velocity = (var('tenant_' ~ tenant ~ '_velocity') | default(0)) | int %}
  {% if velocity > 10000 %}
    {{ return('MERGE') }}
  {% else %}
    {{ return('FULL_REFRESH') }}
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate per-tenant path selection across tenants in CI?
- What monitoring would you add to detect misrouting or latency spikes in adaptive paths?
